Section B

            (a)         Most candidates could not identify the measures for reducing the impact of flooding.
                        Answer
                        Ensure that there is a good understanding of past trends in the rainfall patterns and flooding in the area;
                        Test new production areas ensure that they are not more vulnerable to flood damage before production;
                        Choose the best varieties and breeds that can adapt to change;
                        Take out an insurance against natural disasters such as flooding;
                        Store food for periods of floods
                        Install grass strips near to watercourses and ditches (riparian strips);
                        Ensure a network of ditches, or drainage channels are installed and maintained;
                        Construction of dams to store/ to capture water or construction of dykes to divert water flow;

            (b)         Most candidates could score the maximum marks.  However, a few could not describe how the
                        method maintains water security by giving the general definition of the methods.

        Answer:
        Ensure that there is a good understanding of past trends in the rainfall patterns and flooding in the area;
        Test new production areas to ensure that they are not more vulnerable to flood damage before production;
        Choose the best varieties and breeds that can adapt to change;
        Take out an insurance against natural disasters such as flooding;
        Store food for periods of floods
        Install grass strips near to watercourses and ditches (riparian strips);
        Ensure a network of ditches, drainage channels are installed and maintained;
        Construction of dams to store capture water or construction of dykes to divert water flow;

