           methods or crops;

           Farmers may refuse to adopt new methods or it may take a long time for them to try new methods;
           Farmers who have had a bad experience with previous extension activities are more likely to resist new
           extension activities;

           Some may reject improved crop varieties due to preferred taste; appearance, etc.;
           Many rural farmers do not want to participate in extension activities because they feel that any increased
           income they generate will be distributed to the family and the community;

