3 (a)      Many candidates do not know the internal structure of a root and could, therefore, not label the
           different parts.  If they do not know the parts, they also cannot give the correct function.

  Answer
           A: Epidermis (with root hair cells) + Function: absorption of water and minerals;
           B: (Root) Cortex + Function: storage (of starch) / transport of water and minerals;
           C: Endodermis + Function: (physiological) barrier / description (controls movement of ions / pathogens /
           blocks apoplast pathway);
           D: Pericycle + Function: secondary growth of the root / growth of lateral roots / provides support and
           strength;
           E: (central) vascular bundle + Function: transport of water and minerals and translocation / transport of
           sucrose and amino acids / transport substances / organic and inorganic substances/molecules / xylem and
           phloem which is the transport system in plants / transport substances;
          Part named correctly and the function correct to be awarded 1 mark
          A root hair / root hair cell for A
          R protection for C and D

 (b) When asked to state an adaptation, it needs to be clear which cell is being referred to and an adaptation
