            stating	that	the	cells	do	not	have	cytoplasm	or	organelles	(which	is	the	reason	for	them	being	dead	cells).

          Answer
          xylem + 2 adaptations
          1 walls of (xylem vessels) impregnated with lignin + impermeable to water;
          2 walls of (xylem vessels) impregnated with lignin +mechanical support;
          3 hollows tubes / no cell organelles + little / no resistance to flow of water;
          4 no end walls + little / no resistance to flow of water;
          5 pits in walls + lateral movement of water;
          6 narrow diameter + for adhesion forces;
          phloem + 2 adaptations;
          7 sieve tube elements (very) little cytoplasm + little resistance to flow of sap / AW;
          8 few organelles/no nucleus + little resistance;
          9 plasmodesmata + little resistance / loading and unloading (of sucrose and amino acids);
          10 sieve plates +allow flow from one tube to another / prevent collapse of sieve tubes / provides stability;
          companion cells + 2 adaptations;
          11 many mitochondria + to release energy for loading of cell/active transport;

